    tests/bot-m5: O-3 loud-fail guard (CCR rcv5-vs-main-1a61b36 F-1, D-HOE-20261030-08)
    
    bot-m5 layers its own golden/streak/tapCoins/Broody/abilities/pause model on the real step()/apply().
    run() now throws when a stack with `on` meets any of those src m4.flags.* on (src flagOn: m4.enabled and
    flag === 1), so verify --profile m5x-casual, windowGate and scripts/bot-m5x.ts fail loudly instead of
    double-counting. Flags-off behaviour is unchanged (pure check, shipped flags are all 0).
    
    Tests (fixture CSV b48be8a4 with sha256 assert, D-HOE-20261030-05): per-flag throw, either-alone runs,
    m4.enabled=0 runs, unmodelled flags run, the review's runVerify/windowGate repro, and the verify CLI
    exiting 1 with the O-3 reason instead of the generic exit 4.

